# ── Rust build artifacts ─────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/

# ── cargo-fuzz (libFuzzer) generated outputs ─────────
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

# ── Native libs (libtorch etc. — never commit) ───────
/libtorch/
*.dylib
*.so
*.so.*
*.dll

# ── Handoff / backup cruft ───────────────────────────
_to_delete/
*.tar.gz

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Env / secrets ────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — commit it.
#   Reproducibility is a core project value (pinned deps -> reproducible divergences).
# NOTE: findings/*.json are intentionally NOT ignored — reproducible bug reports
#   are valuable artifacts worth version-controlling.
*.md
skills/
!README.md
# A campaign's triage index belongs with the reports it describes: it records which
# problems a run found, how many cases matched each, and whether they still reproduce.
# The blanket *.md rule above would otherwise drop it.
findings/runs/*
!findings/runs/**/TRIAGE.md